@Zwelf Can we get to the bottom of this? It's not only servers with bad internet connections, but even within the same data center as the database server there are ranks being stored in sqlite every day. I feel like we are missing something obvious, like keeping the mysql connection open, or retrying the connection to mysql first when the previous one failed, before writing to sqlite.

The current approach leads to many thousands of ranks per day being inserted a day late, and players are worried that their rank might not count.

While at it, we could also unify the read/write mysql connections again, maybe having a writer-only connection that is extremely rarely used leads to problems like this.

@Zwelf any idea? Reported by Dan_cao. Works for me on Arch Linux.
